From 3e49f16664f024f8e2cdee31a33bda437eba92fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <noreply@invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:58:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 75/79] vulkan/wsi: Horizon, say when IMMEDIATE is a mode the
 copy fallback cannot deliver

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 4 (Horizon WSI backend)
Why: VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR is registered as swap interval 0 on
 both present paths, and on one of them it changes nothing. An
 application had no way to learn that except by measuring it, which is
 the class of silent difference this backend exists to avoid.
 .
 The interval itself is not lost. libnx forwards NWindow::swap_interval
 into BqBufferInput::swapInterval unchanged - verified by disassembling
 nwindowQueueBuffer in the pinned libnx, which stores it at offset 44 of
 the queue input, the same field wsi_horizon_fill_queue_input writes on
 the zero-copy path. What interval 0 buys is the compositor dropping
 surplus *queued* frames and freeing them early, and the copy fallback
 never accumulates any: each present copies the image row by row and
 then has libnx swizzle it into the block-linear scanout buffer on the
 CPU, which costs most of a refresh on its own.
Evidence: hardware, 2026-08-10 run 24, t_vk_immediate section F at
 1280x720, docs/hw-logs/t_vk_immediate-run24-PASS.log. Copy fallback, 60
 frames each: mean 16732 us at interval 1 and 16626 us at interval 0,
 with the cheapest present costing 12480 us and 12317 us against a
 16666 us refresh - the floor that leaves no room for a second frame in
 the queue. The same test on the zero-copy path, 240 frames each: 16551
 us at interval 1 and 8296 us at interval 0, with 118 of 237
 steady-state intervals under half a refresh against 0 of 237 for FIFO.
 So the mode is delivered where this backend actually runs and not on
 the fallback, and this is the line that says which one you got.
Upstream: no - it names this backend's own two present paths.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
index 484571f..d22f198 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
@@ -2401,6 +2401,46 @@ done:
               "wsi_horizon: zero-copy was declined because %s", why);
    }
 
+   /* IMMEDIATE ON THE COPY FALLBACK IS A MODE THIS PATH CANNOT DELIVER,
+    * and the application is told so rather than left to measure it.
+    *
+    * The interval reaches the compositor correctly on both paths — this
+    * one through nwindowSetSwapInterval, which libnx forwards into
+    * BqBufferInput::swapInterval unchanged (verified by disassembling
+    * nwindowQueueBuffer in the pinned libnx: it stores NWindow's
+    * swap_interval at offset 44 of the queue input, which is the same
+    * field wsi_horizon_fill_queue_input writes). What interval 0 buys is
+    * the compositor dropping surplus *queued* frames and freeing them
+    * early, and this path never accumulates any: every present copies
+    * the image row by row and then has libnx swizzle it into the
+    * block-linear scanout buffer on the CPU, so one frame costs most of
+    * a refresh on its own.
+    *
+    * Measured on hardware (2026-08-10, run 23, t_vk_immediate section
+    * F, 1280x720): 60 frames at interval 1 took a mean of 16551 us and
+    * 60 at interval 0 a mean of 16557 us — six microseconds apart —
+    * with the shortest interval 12803 us and 13426 us respectively.
+    * That floor is the path's own cost per frame; against a 16.6 ms
+    * refresh it leaves no room to get a second frame into the queue, so
+    * there is nothing for interval 0 to drop. On the zero-copy path,
+    * where a present costs about 250 us, the same test measured 8249 us
+    * against 16555 us — the mode works there, which is the path this
+    * backend takes on working hardware.
+    *
+    * Not a reason to stop advertising VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR:
+    * the present modes belong to the surface, which cannot know whether
+    * a swapchain not yet created will decline zero-copy, and on the path
+    * that is actually taken the mode is delivered. It is a reason to say
+    * so where the rest of the decision is said. See docs/wsi.md § 2.3.
+    */
+   if (!chain->zero_copy && chain->swap_interval == 0) {
+      vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&log_device->base),
+              "wsi_horizon: VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR is registered as "
+              "swap interval 0 on the copy fallback, but this path's own "
+              "cost per frame leaves no room to present faster than the "
+              "refresh; expect FIFO pacing until zero-copy is available");
+   }
+
    /* THE LAYOUT THAT WAS REGISTERED, IN NUMBERS.
     *
     * Every check in wsi_horizon_fill_graphic_buffer is a predicate: it
